{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791039132,"nonce":"AtU204vv6UWDV2aMJn7z5nZABl8=","title":"shadow-inner draws an outer shadow","message":"Tw's shadow-inner (theme token shadowInner, e.g. Shadow(0, 2, 4, 0, …)) is drawn as an ordinary drop shadow under the element, because neither ashui's Shadow nor Blinc's (blinc_core layer.rs Shadow: offset, blur, spread, colour) has an inset flag, and RenderProps.shadow entries are all painted as outer shadows. Blinc's inner shadow exists only as the canvas-level draw_inner_shadow.\n\nAsked blinc-b1 for Shadow.inset (default false) and for Blinc's paint walk to draw inset entries over the fill and under the border, clipped to the rounded box.\n\nThen in ashui: an inset field on ashui.types.Shadow passed through Value::Shadow; the theme's shadowInner tokens set it; the display list emits inset shadows after the fill (CSS order) with the local clip of the node's own box; ShadowShader ports Blinc's sdf_shadow inner type. Render probe: a white box with shadow-inner darker just inside its top edge and unchanged outside it.","files":null}]}